{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794368796,"nonce":"KgG3/lrByTVm91vpf0LyBOQj3cc=","message":"Idle commits with the keep-alive off: a window with nothing going on commits every 401 ms, which is the cursor blink (2.5 per second). In a virtual KWin with the pointer moving over the text field the rate rises to about 6 per second; moving the pointer over empty background leaves it at 2.5. Cause: a pointer move that reaches a node with a registered pointer handler (the text input has one for drag selection) marks the frame dirty and requests a redraw (windowed/event_loop/input.rs, pointer_event_to_handler), whether or not anything changed. Not changed: custom pointer handlers (canvas hover drawing) rely on it. Possible follow-up: let a text input register its move handler only while a button is held, or redraw on a move only when the hover target changed. Done in fs-blinc-4-candidate (fork): keep-alive default off (Wayland only), backoff and log for failed acquires, frame.rs comment, restyle test.","files":null}]}